From 79fe9340d659955197514be2adf92560975ccee2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:18:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Thread pools: checks once, all tasks completed before an
 error

- the forms taking a thread pool check the material data view, the
  inputs and the outputs once in the calling thread; the tasks only check
  their workspace and their range of points.
- all the tasks are completed before an exception is reported: a task
  which failed no longer leaves the other tasks reading the objects of the
  calling function after its return.
- the behaviour of a material data view is checked not to be null before
  being used, and the workspace is checked whatever the interface of the
  behaviour.
